2026-11-02T00:19:11.1362910Z [36;1m# Config File[0m
2026-11-02T00:19:11.1363026Z [36;1m# Defaults[0m
2026-11-02T00:19:11.1363132Z [36;1m#[0m
2026-11-02T00:19:11.1363365Z [36;1m# As noted above defaults are awkward to handle as GitHub Actions will inject those values as the input[0m
2026-11-02T00:19:11.1363774Z [36;1m# if the caller doesn't provide them, thus if the input matches the default we don't set it as we[0m
2026-11-02T00:19:11.1364259Z [36;1m# can't tell the difference.  Plus if we did set it when it was the default value then it could potentially[0m
2026-11-02T00:19:11.1364800Z [36;1m# override an external environment variable, or something in the callers configuration file, which then wouldn't[0m
2026-11-02T00:19:11.1365158Z [36;1m# match the configuration priority that is documented.[0m
2026-11-02T00:19:11.1365355Z [36;1mset_env_var_if_provided() {[0m
2026-11-02T00:19:11.1365497Z [36;1m  local var_name="$1"[0m
2026-11-02T00:19:11.1365628Z [36;1m  local input_value="$2"[0m
2026-11-02T00:19:11.1365768Z [36;1m  local default_value="$3"[0m
2026-11-02T00:19:11.1365901Z [36;1m[0m
2026-11-02T00:19:11.1366062Z [36;1m  if [ -n "$input_value" ] && [ "$input_value" != "$default_value" ]; then[0m
2026-11-02T00:19:11.1366348Z [36;1m    # If action was provided with explicit input by the caller set that[0m
2026-11-02T00:19:11.1366660Z [36;1m    # Use printf %q to safely escape special characters and prevent command injection[0m
2026-11-02T00:19:11.1366975Z [36;1m    printf 'export %s=%q\n' "$var_name" "$input_value" >> trivy_envs.txt[0m
2026-11-02T00:19:11.1367293Z [36;1m  fi[0m
2026-11-02T00:19:11.1367387Z [36;1m}[0m
2026-11-02T00:19:11.1367479Z [36;1m[0m
2026-11-02T00:19:11.1367636Z [36;1m# Set environment variables, handling those with default values[0m
2026-11-02T00:19:11.1367982Z [36;1m# cf. https://aquasecurity.github.io/trivy/latest/docs/configuration/#environment-variables[0m
