2026-11-02T00:26:10.9337780Z [36;1m# Defaults[0m
2026-11-02T00:26:10.9337896Z [36;1m#[0m
2026-11-02T00:26:10.9338159Z [36;1m# As noted above defaults are awkward to handle as GitHub Actions will inject those values as the input[0m
2026-11-02T00:26:10.9338612Z [36;1m# if the caller doesn't provide them, thus if the input matches the default we don't set it as we[0m
2026-11-02T00:26:10.9339183Z [36;1m# can't tell the difference.  Plus if we did set it when it was the default value then it could potentially[0m
2026-11-02T00:26:10.9339685Z [36;1m# override an external environment variable, or something in the callers configuration file, which then wouldn't[0m
2026-11-02T00:26:10.9340237Z [36;1m# match the configuration priority that is documented.[0m
2026-11-02T00:26:10.9340474Z [36;1mset_env_var_if_provided() {[0m
2026-11-02T00:26:10.9340637Z [36;1m  local var_name="$1"[0m
2026-11-02T00:26:10.9340787Z [36;1m  local input_value="$2"[0m
